  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>ode workflows</keyword>
  <short_description>ODE examples and object workflow.</short_description>
  <description>
    <p>The function workflow returns arrays or a solution structure. The object workflow stores the problem in an <b>ode</b> instance and returns a result object from <b>solve</b>.</p>
    <table style="width:100%">
  <tr><th>Workflow</th><th>Main calls</th><th>When to use</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Function</td><td><b>ode45</b>, <b>ode15s</b>, <b>ode15i</b></td><td>Compact scripts that return arrays or a solution structure.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Object</td><td><b>ode</b>, <b>solve</b>, <b>deval</b></td><td>Reusable problem definitions with solver options and result objects.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Post-processing</td><td><b>deval</b>, <b>odextend</b></td><td>Interpolate or continue a computed solution.</td></tr>
</table>
    <p>Use a solution structure with <b>deval</b> for interpolation and <b>odextend</b> to continue an integration. Use <b>Events</b> to locate zero crossings, <b>Mass</b> for mass matrix systems, and <b>Jacobian</b> to help stiff solvers.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Function workflow with interpolation.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[sol = ode45(@(t,y) -y, [0 1], 1);
yhalf = deval(sol, 0.5)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Object workflow.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[problem = ode('ODEFcn', @(t,y) -y, 'InitialValue', 1);
result = solve(problem, 0, 1);
value = deval(result, 0.5)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Refined output and statistics.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[options = odeset('Refine', 4, 'Stats', 'on');
[t, y] = ode45(@(t,y) y, [0 1], 1, options)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
